## 4. Structural observations
Hemoglobin beta is a globin-family protein with a compact globin fold dominated by alpha-helical secondary structure[span_18](start_span)[span_18](end_span). In native adult hemoglobin, beta-globin associates with two alpha-globin chains to form an alpha2beta2 tetramer[span_19](start_span)[span_19](end_span). The beta chain participates in oxygen transport as part of hemoglobin; its biological context includes a heme cofactor, but a protein-only predicted model should not automatically be interpreted as a complete experimentally assembled hemoglobin complex[span_20](start_span)[span_20](end_span).

