## 5. Model confidence and limitations
The RCSB record for the computed AlphaFold model AF_AFP68871F1 reports a global pLDDT confidence score of 97.18 and 147 modeled residues[span_21](start_span)[span_21](end_span). PLDDT is a per-residue estimate of local prediction confidence, not an experimental resolution and not proof that every biological interaction is represented[span_22](start_span)[span_22](end_span). The model page notes that the computed model does not have experimental data verifying its accuracy[span_23](start_span)[span_23](end_span). The structure should therefore be described as a prediction, not as a newly solved experimental structure[span_24](start_span)[span_24](end_span).

