## 7. Conclusion
The AlphaFold model provides a useful structural hypothesis for human beta-globin[span_35](start_span)[span_35](end_span). Its compact globin fold is consistent with the known role of the protein as one chain of hemoglobin[span_36](start_span)[span_36](end_span)[span_37](start_span)[span_37](end_span). The model's high reported global confidence supports using it for educational visualization, while biological assembly, ligand placement and experimental validation should be considered separately[span_38](start_span)[span_38](end_span)[span_39](start_span)[span_39](end_span).

